  "map_info": {
    "name": "02 The Trace",
    "lookup_name": "Point_Context",
    "description": "Explores the trace as duration before form. Movement leaves an accumulated imprint that has no fixed geometry until it is captured. This map foregrounds time and embodiment as conditions of geometrical appearance, before any line or shape is yet defined.",
    "description_2": "The Trace introduces duration and embodied residue into geometry. Unlike points and lines that resolve instantly into abstraction, traces accumulate over time as records of movement. The map emphasizes gesture, repetition, and error, foregrounding how space remembers interaction. The trace resists full discretization, functioning as a counterpoint to the clean logic of primitives and revealing geometry as a lived process rather than a static system.",
